# Mobile Guidelines

## Native UX
- Respect iOS and Android safe areas (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`).
- Handle keyboard so focused inputs remain visible.
- Support Android hardware back through the shared back-button hook.
- Use touch-friendly controls (roughly ≥ 44px targets).

## Capacitor practices
- Encapsulate Capacitor APIs in reusable utilities/services.
- Avoid calling plugins directly from feature UI.
- Prefer shared cross-platform behavior; branch by platform only when required.
- Plan for offline and poor-network states (banners, cached content, disabled actions).

## Verification
- Validate status bar, keyboard, back navigation, and safe areas on both iOS and Android.
- After native plugin or config changes, rebuild web assets and run `cap sync` before device checks.
- Treat haptics and status-bar updates as best-effort; never block core UX if a plugin fails.
- Persist only appropriate preferences via Capacitor Preferences (theme, settings), never secrets in plain storage without a deliberate security design.
